      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-03-28_WidnesExaminer_art0094" n="art0094">
        <head>JAMESON'S RIDE.</head>
        <p>JAMESON'S RIDE.</p>
        <p>Authentic records of this Historical Evetat now reach Ergland, and the Crisis is virtually over. Peace and plenty again rule through the Gold3n Territory of the 'lransvaal, and the act of Dr. Jameson links this modern Hero inalienably to one of the Historic Incideuts of the Century. No infringement of our neutrality can be urged, against us in laying bare to the Liverpool public a subtee,t of strong local interest and advantage. A rumour was current previously, hat is only con- firmed with" Dr. Jim's arrival, ttett his taave band of Volunteers had become possessed (prior to the Raid) of the redoubtable clothiog manufactured especially for South Africa by Messrs. HESOCHS- BEIM lt ELLIS, UNIVERSITY HOUSE, Islington, Liverpool, and that the Natural Wool Under- wear famous for awls climates, shipped to the South African Repuplic, as well as to the Char- tered Company's territory, by Messrs. lIENOCHS- BhEG &amp; IsLLIS, was worn by the Doctor's helps during their trying time. The Government Serges (passing full test for shades, dyes, end streagth) are kept ill stock at University Hou c. HENOCHSBERG &amp; ELLIS are prepared to under- take and execute ORDERS for GENTLEMEN'S SUITS f,.r 505., tor YOUTIIS' SUITS 355., and for Boys' SUITS 255., from the exact materials, of which they now hold a good selection, as the contract for the betel Government is in course of completiota by this well-kuown firm.</p>
      </div>
