        <p>Mucn WOOLTON DISTRICT COUNCIL ELXCTION, 1896. To TEE ELECTORS OF MUCH WOOLTON. We have nominated Mr. Eustace Carey as a Candidate for Election to the Much Woolton Urban District Council, isa place of Mr. Ellinson, who has retired. Mr. Carey has consented to the nomination, and we feel strongly that. if elected, his experience of Sanitary and other work, which he has acquired by 18 years' service on the Widnes Local Board, will be of great advantage to the Rate- payers of Much Woolton. We therefore ask your vote and Interest on his behalf at the Election, which takes place on Monday, 30th instant, from 8 a.m. to 8 p.m., at the St. Peter's Schoolroom, Church Road South, Woolton. GEORGE BEAUMONT, WILLIAM 11. TATE, WILLIAM TOD, RICLIARD BULMAN. Woolton, 18th March, 1396.</p>
